          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If an amount is increased by the same percentage each time, powers can be used. For example: 50 increased by 12% three times would be:",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p8-q9-demonstration",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "center",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}50\\times1.12\\times1.12\\times1.12\\\\&=50\\times(1.12)^3\\\\&=70.25\\text{ (2 d.p.)}\\end{aligned}",
              "display": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p8-q9-instruction-paragraph",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Use a similar technique to find the final value in these situations. Round to 2 decimal places.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p8-q9-a-node",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "The mass of a rat initially at 60 grams grows at a rate of 10% every month for 3 months.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "79.86 g",
          "worked": "The monthly multiplier is $1+0.10=1.10$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Final mass}&=60\\times(1.10)^3\\\\&=79.86\\text{ g}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q9-b-node",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "The cost of a new car initially at $\\$80\\,000$ increases by 5% every year for 4 years.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\$97\\,240.50$",
          "worked": "The yearly multiplier is $1+0.05=1.05$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Final cost}&=80\\,000\\times(1.05)^4\\\\&=\\$97\\,240.50\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q9-c-node",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "The value of a house initially at $\\$380\\,000$ decreases by 4% per year for 7 years.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\$285\\,550.04$",
          "worked": "The yearly multiplier is $1-0.04=0.96$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Final value}&=380\\,000\\times(0.96)^7\\\\&\\approx\\$285\\,550.04\\end{align*}$$\nRounded to 2 decimal places.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q9-d-node",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "The length of a pencil initially at 16 cm decreases through being sharpened by 15% every week for 5 weeks.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "7.10 cm",
          "worked": "The weekly multiplier is $1-0.15=0.85$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Final length}&=16\\times(0.85)^5\\\\&\\approx7.10\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$\nRounded to 2 decimal places.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
  },
